+## Work runtimes
+
+Each confirmed Work can run this project **in parallel** with the
+default runtime. Designate the target Work by its Work Root directory
+(or its `main` checkout) through `DIR`:
+
+```bash
+make DIR=.worktrees/feat/schema-preview work-up       # start the Work runtime
+make DIR=.worktrees/feat/schema-preview work-status   # show its containers
+make DIR=.worktrees/feat/schema-preview work-config   # render resolved compose config (dry run)
+make DIR=.worktrees/feat/schema-preview work-run ARGS="npm test"  # run a command inside it
+make DIR=.worktrees/feat/schema-preview work-down     # stop it (volumes kept)
+make DIR=.worktrees/feat/schema-preview work-cleanup  # down + remove the Work DB volume (destructive)
+```
+
+`DIR` is only a path locator. `scripts/work-runtime.sh` resolves it to
+the confirmed Work identity `<work-type>/<work-name>` (tracked
+`documents/` plus the registered `main` checkout must exist), then all
+lifecycle commands derive resource identities from that Work identity
+through `scripts/resource-identity.js`:
+
+| Resource | Scope | Work runtime value |
+|---|---|---|
+| toolchain image | project (shared) | `work-runtime-dev:node20` — same as default |
+| package cache volume | project (shared) | `work-runtime-resources-pkg-cache` — same as default |
+| DB/data volume | per Work | `work-runtime-resources-<work-slug>-db-data` |
+| host port | per Work | deterministic from the Work identity (30000–49999) |
+| Compose project / containers / network | per Work | `work-runtime-resources-<work-slug>[…]` |
+
+`<work-slug>` is the Work identity lowercased with non-alphanumerics
+mapped to `-` (e.g. `feat/schema-preview` → `feat-schema-preview`).
+Derivation is deterministic — no random names and no new Work identity
+per run — so `work-up`, `work-status`, `work-down`, and `work-cleanup`
+always resolve the same resource set for the same Work. `work-cleanup`
+removes only the Work-scoped DB volume; the shared image and cache are
+never touched.
+
 ## Verification
 
 - `make verify` — host entry point; runs the project verification inside
